# Huawei Y6 2019 (MRD-LX1) — MT6761 (Helio A22)
#
# Port notes:
# Stock LK analyzed statically (ARM bootstrap + Thumb body, load address
# 0x48000000). All addresses below were identified by behavior
# (call-graph + instruction pattern analysis of the stock LK image),
# mirroring the field set of the MT6761 "t482l" port (PR #94).
#
# Field-by-field status:
#   CONFIRMED (call-graph / pattern verified in the stock image):
#     BOOTLOADER_BASE/SIZE  — LK header
#     PLATFORM_INIT(_CALLER) — single caller of the platform init fn
#     INIT_STORAGE(_CALLER)  — single caller + storage-driver bl chain
#     DPRINTF/MALLOC/FREE    — hot call targets, verified bodies
#     FASTBOOT_*             — fastboot string printers/register/publish
#     MTK_DETECT_KEY         — keycode cmps 0x47/8/0x11
#     PARTITION_GET_INDEX    — 0x4804ef0c: name->index loop over the
#                              24-byte pt entries, strncmp vs entry name
#                              ptr, 18 callers incl. the flash handler
#     PARTITION_GET_OFFSET   — 0x4804f054: idx*24 entry walk,
#                              umull(start, blocksize) -> 64-bit offset
#     PARTITION_GET_SIZE     — 0x4804ef74: idx*24 entry walk, returns
#                              entry size; used as the 3rd step of the
#                              LK's own flash: handler (idx,offset,size)
#     MT_PART_GET_DEVICE     — 0x48051dbc: returns *device_global
#                              (0x48174a82); device struct:
#                              [4]=init flag [0x10]=write [0x14]=read
#     THREAD_CREATE/RESUME, VIDEO_PRINTF, APP, LK_LOG_STORE — pattern
#                              matches, plausible call contexts
#   NEEDS VERIFY:
#     BOOTMODE_ADDRESS — a .bss int (bootmode enum) that the LK reads
#       in its boot-mode-select path and fastboot path. No unique
#       static signature found without a decompiler. Locate it starting
#       from the fastboot continue path (0x4802EBE0-0x4802EC34: the fn
#       checking the "fastboot active" flag and dispatching to the
#       fastboot loop vs. normal boot); the bootmode int global is read
#       near there. Candidate from the early-boot flow: 0x4817747c
#       (.bss, read from the main boot flow at 0x48003d2a and from
#       fastboot-region code at 0x4802edfc) — used below, UNVERIFIED.
#
